X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/southern-appalachian-birds-through-the-seasons/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260430T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260430T160000
DTSTAMP:20260421T043254
CREATED:20260313T155132Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260313T155132Z
UID:10016997-1777550400-1777564800@www.ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Southern Appalachian Birds Through the Seasons
DESCRIPTION:Southern Appalachian Birds Through the Seasons\nwith Carlton Burke \nThursday\, April 30  |  12 – 4pm \nBRN – Core \nREGISTER HERE \nSince birds are capable of long distance flights and many engage in annual migration rituals\, their presence in our area often changes in relation to the seasons of the year.  In this class we will discuss the seasonal patterns of southern Appalachian birds and focus on some of the major species and their annual life cycles. As part of this program\, there will be a “lab” portion where students will be able to meet some live birds and participate in other hands-on components to deepen the learning. \nCarlton Burke is a naturalist and educator who operates Carolina Mountain Naturalists\, an educational service which offers wildlife and nature educational programs throughout western North Carolina. He also was on the staff of the western North Carolina Nature Center in Asheville for over 25 years as the Curator of Exhibits. Carlton co-hosts a weekly radio program NATURE NEWS and is also a NC state and federally licensed wildlife rehabilitator. \n\nMembers: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions.\nSee a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs.\nWe are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide.\nFollow us on Facebook & Instagram!\nJoin our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord!\nInterested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here.\n\nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/southern-appalachian-birds-through-the-seasons/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/pexels-chris-f-38966-2992549.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Avl Digital Nomads": "https://www.meetup.com/avl-digital-nomads/events/313943905/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_avl_digital_nomads
X-SOURCE:AVL Digital Nomads
UID:event_313943905@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260421T141740Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260430T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260430T150000
SUMMARY:Volunteer opportunity @ Manna Food Bank
DESCRIPTION:AVL Digital Nomads\n## **AVL Digital Nomads Volunteer Day at M
 ANNA FoodBank**\n\n## **Hunger hides in plain sight in Asheville and surro
 unding communities.**\n\nMany of our neighbors are struggling in silence 
 — facing empty shelves and impossible choices.\nLet’s show up and do s
 omething about it.\nJoin **AVL Digital Nomads** for a volunteer shift at *
 *MANNA FoodBank**\, where we’ll work together to:\n\n* Sort donations\n*
  Bag bulk food items\n* Date-check perishable goods\n* Support the team ke
 eping our community fed\n\nTogether\, we can help create a more caring Ash
 eville where no one goes without a meal.\n\n***\n\n## **What to Expect**\n
 \nIf it’s your first time volunteering at MANNA\, here’s a quick walkt
 hrough:\n\n* Plan to arrive a few minutes early at the former FedEx wareho
 use\n* Turn left into the **volunteer parking lot**\n* Walk past the turns
 tile fence and enter the warehouse\n* Continue down the hallway past the b
 athrooms and fridges\n* You’ll find a small lounge area with high-top ta
 bles where volunteers gather\n\nMANNA staff will usually greet you somewhe
 re between the parking lot and the lounge.\nThere will be individual volun
 teers in addition to our group\, so:\n\n* Look for other **AVL Digital Nom
 ads**\n* Introduce yourself and connect with new arrivals\n* We’ll coord
 inate with simple name tags\n\nOnce everyone is checked in:\n\n* MANNA sta
 ff will give a **brief safety overview**\n* Then assign tasks for the day\
 n\nThey are very accommodating\, and there are usually multiple types of t
 asks available if you have any limitations.\n\n***\n\n## **Important Detai
 ls (Please Read)**\n\n### Location\n\nMANNA FoodBank\n99 Broadpointe Drive
 \, Mills River\, NC\n*Doors open 10 minutes before the shift — **please 
 arrive a 15 minutes early**.*\n\n### Liability Waiver\n\n* Waivers will be
  provided **on-site**\n* All volunteers must sign upon arrival\n* Voluntee
 rs 17 and under require a parent or guardian signature\n\n### Dress Code\n
 \n* **Closed-toe shoes are required** (no exceptions)\n* Wear comfortable 
 clothes you don’t mind getting a little dirty\n\n### What to Bring\n\n* 
 Water or your preferred beverage\n* Light snacks will be available\n\n### 
 Guidelines\n\nTo maintain a safe and welcoming environment:\n\n* **Nicotin
 e-Free Facility**\n* No smoking\, vaping\, or nicotine use inside or withi
 n fenced areas\n* Items must be stored in your vehicle\n* Designated smoki
 ng area is at the far end of the parking lot\n* **Substance-Free Workplace
 **\n* No alcohol\, drugs\, or impairing substances (including THC/Kratom)\
 n* **Age Requirement**\n* Volunteers must be **10 years or older**\n\nThis
  is a great opportunity to connect with the AVL Digital Nomads community w
 hile giving back in a meaningful way.\nCome be part of it
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/avl-digital-nomads/events/313943905/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260325T155542Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260325T155542Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
