BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Asheville Runners": "https://www.meetup.com/asheville-runners/events/312835125/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_asheville_runners
X-SOURCE:Asheville Runners
UID:event_312835125@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260421T141739Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260430T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260430T200000
SUMMARY:Thursday Run 
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Runners\nCome run 1\, 3\, or 6 miles and stay for a 
 beer and soccer tennis after at Olde London Road.\n\nRoutes-\n1 miler:\nRI
 GHT out of OLR parking lot\nContinue around roundabout at Clingman\, and h
 ead toward the river on Lyman St.\nRIGHT on River Arts Place\nCross Rivers
 ide onto the Greenway\nRight on the Greenway to the Craven St Park put in 
 (the dock)\nTurn around and go back the same way to OLR\n\n3 miler:\nStart
  the same as 1 miler\nContinue onto Craven St. Bridge\nLEFT onto Greenway 
 after bridge\nFollow Greenway all the way until it ends at Haywood Rd.\nRI
 GHT onto Haywood Rd\, go across the bridge\nCross the Roundabout at Robert
 s St. and continue onto Clingman\nContinue on Clingman\nLEFT onto Owens Be
 ll Lane\nLEFT onto Hilliard at the top of the hill\nLEFT onto W Haywood\, 
 follow all the way down to Roberts\nLEFT onto Roberts\nFollow Roberts back
  to OLR\nPass OLR to Bartlett\, turn around and come back to OLR\n\n6 mile
 r:\nAfter the W Haywood downhill to Roberts\nLEFT onto Roberts St. take to
  Lyman and head back to the Greenway\nLEFT onto the Greenway\, take all th
 e way to Amboy\nRIGHT on Amboy to cross the bridge\nRIGHT into French Broa
 d River Park\, run the loop at the park\nCross back over the bridge on Amb
 oy and run the Greenway back to the roundabout\nFollow Lyman back to OLR
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-runners/events/312835125/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260111T194414Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260111T194414Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/four-hand-piano-trio/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260430T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260430T203000
DTSTAMP:20260421T101736
CREATED:20260216T140706Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260331T164712Z
UID:10006519-1777573800-1777581000@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Four-Hand Piano Trio
DESCRIPTION:AmiciMusic continues their Music at the Museum series with a program entitled Four-Hand Piano Trio on Thursday\, April 30 at 6:30pm. \nThe concert features an international ensemble of musicians—Vadim Tchikil\, violin (from France/Russia)\, Jacques-Pierre Malan\, cello (from South Africa)\, Francesco Cipolletta\, piano (from Italy)\, and pianist/artistic director Daniel Weiser. \nThey will perform a program featuring exciting music for violin\, cello\, and four-hand piano\, a very rare and unique combination.  They will play two of the four quartets by Romantic composer Hermann Berens for this combination\, as well as some spirited arrangements of the Brahms Hungarian Dances and Liszt’s Rhapsody no. 2. \nAmiciMusic is an award-winning non-profit chamber music organization dedicated to performing intimate\, high-quality concerts in non-traditional spaces and to breaking down barriers between performers and audiences through fun\, informative talks before each piece is played.  It should be a spectacular show you will not want to miss! \nPurchase Tickets \n  \nThe Steinway piano is available to the Asheville Art Museum through the courtesy of the Asheville Chamber Music Series.
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/four-hand-piano-trio/
LOCATION:NC
CATEGORIES:Performance
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/Dan-Weiser-Large-1-1-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Meetup Group Ssbjicnx": "https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-ssbjicnx/events/bnlxwtyjcgbnc/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_meetup_group_ssbjicnx
X-SOURCE:Dodgeball AVL
UID:event_bnlxwtyjcgbnc@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260421T141744Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260430T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260430T220000
SUMMARY:Dodgeball Open Play (ages 21+)
DESCRIPTION:Dodgeball AVL\n**This is an outdoor event so weather can affec
 t our Meetup. We do not play in rain\, temps below 40F\, or other adverse 
 weather conditions. Keep on eye on the weather and check group updates to 
 stay informed. ** Waitlisted players\, please still consider attending! 
 We only sit players if games have reached capacity. That’s 12v12 for one
  court and 11v11 for 2 courts. We usually have less people at the beginnin
 g after setup (~7:15pm) and the end of the night (after 9pm). That said\, 
 we are growing in attendance so play time is not guaranteed for the waitli
 st and those who do not sign up. Ready to dodge\, duck\, dip\, dive\, an
 d dodge? Come show us what you got with Asheville’s weekly pick-up dodge
 ball group! We're hosting open play on Thursday night at Asheville Sport
 s Club. We are all about having a great time and getting that adrenaline p
 umping! Friendly competition is always welcome but fun\, safety\, and resp
 ect for all players are the top priorities. We use squishy rubber dodgebal
 ls that are fun to throw and catch but can sting with enough velocity so n
 o headshots are allowed. Throws should aim at your target’s shoulders or
  lower. No experience is necessary - we'll teach you the rules. Open to 
 adults 21 and up (bring your ID!). We’re sorry but we cannot accommodate
  teens or children because there is alcohol on the premises and no one wan
 ts to be the person who accidentally hurts a kid. Sign waivers at the bar 
 before playing and enjoy a beverage between games. Rules of the game are
  covered at the start of the event so please be there at 7pm to learn our 
 format. We loosely follow the USA Dodgeball ruleset with some exceptions t
 o help new players adapt to the game more quickly. Check out our brief rul
 es and expectations summary attached as photos to this Meetup. Here’s 
 an approximate schedule for this event depending on when people arrive: 
 6:50 - 7:10pm* - Set up courts and mingle - help with set up is appreciate
 d! 7:10 - 7:15pm - Rules and announcements 7:15 - 9:30pm - Play! *If
  we have enough people once setup is done\, we’ll jump into rules and an
 nouncements early. We need at least 8 players to start a game\, so take ad
 vantage of the daylight and try to arrive right at the beginning! Since 
 this is a free event\, the more community support we can gather\, the bett
 er experience everyone will have\, especially for the organizers! If you'd
  like to help\, please arrive early or stay late to assist with set up and
  breakdown. This is a free community offering\, however\, if you are fee
 ling generous\, donations are welcomed to help support and expand our grou
 p. We take donations through Pledge here in Meetup or Venmo (dodgeballavl)
 . Cash of course is great too and more effective as there are no platform 
 fees. Your donations genuinely help the group by helping with equipment pu
 rchases and raising funds to eventually add another night of dodgeball in 
 an indoor gym. This event would not be possible without the support of Ash
 eville Sports Club. Please consider generously tipping your bartenders and
  karaoke DJ as well.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-ssbjicnx/events/bnlxwtyj
 cgbnc/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260411T152140Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260411T152140Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
